going from nk=4 to nk=5: nrow(dirs) grows by 1; 'attempted' (forward-pass-complete count) grows by 2

CHECK bb03.1 TRUE fit$nk == min(200,max(20,2p))+1 for every p in {1,5,9,10,11,50,99,100,101,150} at n=60
CHECK bb03.2 TRUE nk is not reduced below the formula for small n (n=10,p=5 and n=30,p=150)
CHECK bb03.3 FALSE HYPOTHESIS nk is reduced for small n (fit$nk < formula in at least one edge case)
CHECK bb03.4 TRUE the forward pass never lets nrow(dirs) exceed nk, for nk in 2..9
CHECK bb03.5 FALSE HYPOTHESIS whenever termcond signals the term limit was reached, nrow(dirs) == nk exactly
CHECK bb03.6 FALSE HYPOTHESIS whenever termcond signals the term limit was reached, the counted terms (forward-pass-complete line) == nk
CHECK bb03.7 TRUE going from nk=4 to nk=5 adds exactly one row to dirs (a single hinge, not a rejected pair)
CHECK bb03.8 FALSE HYPOTHESIS a single-hinge step is counted as 1 (not 2) toward the 'attempted' term budget too (attempted also grows by 1 from nk=4 to nk=5)
CHECK bb03.9 TRUE a single-hinge step is counted as a full pair (2 slots) against the budget even though only 1 real term results (attempted grows by 2, matching Part 2's pattern)
CHECK bb03.10 TRUE for nk = 3..9 the counted terms == nk when (nk-1) is even; attempted == nk-1 when (nk-1) is odd (the forward pass always budgets 2 slots per pair attempt and never spends a lone leftover slot)
